{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1434811-lancea-blood-feuds","id":1434811,"title":"Lancea Blood Feuds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-07T22:12:56-08:00","id":1434811,"title":"Lancea Blood Feuds","content":"Got today a dream. Two older Kindred - Anachilla, if I remember correct term - have a great argument. Quarrel goes by decades now. The only solution from Lancea Sanctum priest is 'God's Judgment' - fight to the death between feuding vampires. Sacred duel, where no other Kindred can interfere. God will choose the winner.<br /> <br /> Just some idea from my dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T14:29:19-08:00","id":1435316,"title":"","content":"Isn't Monocacy (kindred duels) more of an Invictus thing. Perhaps you should look into Savonarola and the burning of the vanities for an appropriate way for the lancea et sanctum to settle it's differences. I heard that Savonarola was defeated in a &quot;monk off&quot; to determine how much god favored him. Try challenges like walking on coals or holy ground or accepting god's judgement through Theban sorcery. Historically trial by combat was more for the nobility. Try dunking in holy water or some other contest of skill, perhaps dueling preachers to a crowd or a debate on theology against an impartial judge. Or it could work in a city with heavy Invictus influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T16:04:41-08:00","id":1435323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laguz 24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1434811-lancea-blood-feuds?p=1435316#post1435316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Monocacy (kindred duels) more of an Invictus thing. Perhaps you should look into Savonarola and the burning of the vanities for an appropriate way for the lancea et sanctum to settle it's differences. I heard that Savonarola was defeated in a &quot;monk off&quot; to determine how much god favored him. Try challenges like walking on coals or holy ground or accepting god's judgement through Theban sorcery. Historically trial by combat was more for the nobility. Try dunking in holy water or some other contest of skill, perhaps dueling preachers to a crowd or a debate on theology against an impartial judge. Or it could work in a city with heavy Invictus influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very fair point.<br /> <br /> L+S \u200bcongregations would probably care far more about somehow showing divine (dis)favor for the individual and one's role as a monster in the service of god than anything else.<br /> <br /> Shows of prowess, martial or not, that has always been more of a macho/bravado/status sensitive thing, one actually opposed (ineffectively) by religious and state institutions through the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-12-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}